---
import DocShell from '../../layouts/doc-shell.astro';
import { docsLinks } from '../../lib/nav';

const toc = [
   { id: 'workflow', label: 'Workflow' },
   { id: 'resume', label: 'Resume and hints' },
   { id: 'claims', label: 'Evidence claims' },
];
---

<DocShell
   title="Audit a full site with an agent"
   summary="The full-site-audit skill coordinates scope, page discovery, sampling decisions, real screen reader checks, and a resumable report bundle."
   links={docsLinks}
   toc={toc}
>
   <section class="panel" id="workflow">
      <h2>Workflow</h2>
      <ol>
         <li>The agent asks whether the target is one page, a section, or a site.</li>
         <li>It runs <code>a1 audit discover</code> and reviews the page inventory.</li>
         <li>Above 50 pages, it asks whether to audit every page or sample shared templates.</li>
         <li>It runs automated page audits, then one real VoiceOver or NVDA session at a time.</li>
         <li>It builds the HTML, PDF, JSON, and EARL reports.</li>
      </ol>
      <p>
         Install the repository's <code>full-site-audit</code> skill through the same
         <a href="/guides/agent-skill">agent skill package</a> as the page-level skill.
      </p>
   </section>

   <section class="panel" id="resume">
      <h2>Resume and hints</h2>
      <p>
         The agent updates <code>inventory.json</code> after each page and phase. A later session
         resumes audited pages without repeating them. Site hints live in
         <code>.a11ied/sites/&lt;origin-key&gt;/hints.json</code>. The agent checks each hint against
         the current site before it uses it.
      </p>
   </section>

   <section class="panel" id="claims">
      <h2>Evidence claims</h2>
      <p>
         Sampled pages stay marked not tested. A partial crawl stays a partial inventory.
         Automated, hybrid, and manual outcomes remain separate. A passing automated result
         is not reported as full WCAG conformance.
      </p>
   </section>
</DocShell>
